### Nginx web server on jump
- First temp rule to allow internet access
  - set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-WAN rule 999 action accept
  - set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-WAN rule 999 source address 172.16.50.4
  - set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-WAN rule 999 description "TEMP - Allow jump to download packages"
  - commit -> save
  - delete when done
- now sudo apt install nginx
- change default index.html file
- now allow port 80 from mgmt01 to jump
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 15 action accept
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 15 protocol tcp
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 15 destination address 172.16.50.4
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 15 destination port 80
commit
save

### Passwordless login
- On win machine
  - ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096
- verify key
  - type C:\Users\azrael\.ssh\id_rsa.pub
- may need to add temp rule on fw between dmz and lan 
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 999 action accept
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 999 protocol tcp
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 999 source address 172.16.150.50
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 999 destination address 172.16.50.4
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 999 destination port 22
set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-DMZ rule 999 description "TEMP - SSH from wks01 to jump"
commit
save
(delete when done)
- Now copy to linux machine
  - scp C:\Users\azrael\.ssh\id_rsa.pub azrael-adm@172.16.50.4:~/ 
- to add key to authorized keys on jump user (cat doesn't work for some reason)
  - sudo tee -a /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh/authorized_keys < ~/id_rsa.pub
- may need to change permissions
  - sudo chmod 600 /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh/authorized_keys
  - sudo chown jump-azrael-passless:jump-azrael-passless /home/jump-azrael-passless/.ssh/authorized_keys
- now test connection
  - from wks ssh jump-azrael-passless@172.16.50.4
  - it should ask for key passphrase
